{
    // Every weapon a player can be given, and the groups they show up in.
    //
    // This is the whole list. There is no way to ask the game which weapons exist, so vMenu reads
    // them from here instead. That also means adding your own addon weapons is easy: put them in
    // one of the groups below, or make a group of your own for them. There is no separate list and
    // no separate menu for addon weapons, they sit right alongside the rest.
    //
    // The name on the left of each group, so "Handguns" or "Melee", is what players see in the
    // menu. Nothing in vMenu depends on these eight groups existing, so delete them and write your
    // own if you would rather.
    //
    // Inside a group, the name on the left is the weapon's spawn name. The text on the right is
    // what shows next to it. If that text happens to be one of the game's own label keys, such as
    // "WT_PIST", the game's own translation of it is shown, which means the menu follows whatever
    // language the player is playing in without you doing anything. Anything else is shown exactly
    // as you wrote it, which is usually what an addon weapon wants.
    //
    // The order in this file is the order in the menu, for the groups and for the weapons inside
    // them. If you want your own weapons at the very top, move their group to the top of this file.
    //
    // Every group also gets its own permission, generated for you when the server starts. The
    // groups below would create these eight:
    //
    //     vMenu.Enhanced.Menus.WeaponOptions.Categories.handguns
    //     vMenu.Enhanced.Menus.WeaponOptions.Categories.assault_rifles
    //     vMenu.Enhanced.Menus.WeaponOptions.Categories.shotguns
    //     vMenu.Enhanced.Menus.WeaponOptions.Categories.sub_light_machine_guns
    //     vMenu.Enhanced.Menus.WeaponOptions.Categories.throwables
    //     vMenu.Enhanced.Menus.WeaponOptions.Categories.melee
    //     vMenu.Enhanced.Menus.WeaponOptions.Categories.heavy_weapons
    //     vMenu.Enhanced.Menus.WeaponOptions.Categories.sniper_rifles
    //
    // As you can see, the permission is your group name in lowercase, with anything that is not a
    // letter, a digit or an underscore turned into an underscore. You never have to write those out
    // yourself: they are listed for you in config/permissions.cfg.example, right next to all the
    // normal ones, each marked with a note saying it came from this file. Granting
    // vMenu.Enhanced.Menus.WeaponOptions.Categories.All grants your own groups too.
    //
    // If you want to hand out one weapon on its own rather than a whole group, put it in the
    // "weapons" list in config/model-whitelists.json instead. It stays in the same place in the
    // menu, it just answers to a permission of its own.
    //
    // A weapon can only be in one group. If you list the same one twice, the first group wins and
    // the server console tells you about it. Spawn names may only contain letters, digits and
    // underscores, because the same name is what a whitelist permission would be named after.
    //
    // weapon_unarmed is deliberately not here. Every player already has it.
    //
    // One thing to keep in mind: the menu is built once when a player joins, so after changing this
    // file you have to restart the resource before anybody sees the difference.

